{"about_the_game":"<p class=\"bb_paragraph\">General Command is a Napoleonic era turn-based war game.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\">Take command of the battle field, and strategically maneuver units based on their strengths and the current battle conditions.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"><u><strong>Units:</strong></u></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3173160/extras/BlueInfantry.png?t=1745036898\" />\u00a0</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"><strong>Infantry</strong> are the foundation of your army.\u00a0 Although slow moving, they start with the most health and have a decent attack range.\u00a0 A few infantry units with concentrated fire will pack quite a punch.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3173160/extras/RedCavalry.png?t=1745036898\" /></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"><strong>Cavalry</strong>\u00a0are the heart of any special maneuvers.\u00a0 They are only effective at attacking in close range, but their ability to traverse the battlefield quickly, and their ability to attack immediately after moving make them great for flanking or charging the enemy.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3173160/extras/CanonShot.png?t=1745036898\" /></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"><strong>Canons</strong> set the tone of the entire battle.\u00a0 They are stationary, but can fire projectiles at long range and rip through enemy lines.\u00a0 Beware of friendly fire, as these units will fire  if an enemy is in their line of sight.</p>","background":"https://store.akamai.steamstatic.com/images/storepagebackground/app/3173160?t=1745036898","background_raw":"